{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-72120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a type II region in two-dimensional space?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/e472070f17c47e78024217ed750690b88de87f3849818368dda1dde5d91d90d4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72120" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4482dfff4474145f9d9376488f2566949daf2ef7994717ff9e1346f596161a6"} {"question" "q-72120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/205fdc7a29c94d36b5bd8847a2600c41d7e3fd2ac0fd92947dddcb241bdae012.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/254691f56d0586b2cbfd75a3fce34ecc1062b0f0fde538d3885860ed1b71555c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/a216b288b70301fb14b8f1219b909edb69ab77b08c29460b5522abc2025ab494.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/edbcc3bcef921ef736f9bd31bec56f69736c632bf835cf4c9c1c46026fda8083.png"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72120" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/a216b288b70301fb14b8f1219b909edb69ab77b08c29460b5522abc2025ab494.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/28290c5530efd27a979f4284481ca7e0384342d7d426dde0ab36894a0d77a166.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/3007cffb725faee44d2a06ad077eec630791b1a94c373a323f62d0d721c87207.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/383f88668435556d3a856cf852caf548b1f1bf3a90d50f9d85d7968188984804.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4482dfff4474145f9d9376488f2566949daf2ef7994717ff9e1346f596161a6"} {"question" "q-72187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-72187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/c316b62d5c1a08c6513413fd87c36c6feb26fb632709909a9c9f761d0806c4af.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-2(x-3)\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/fb05eec73599c1beb8dd588c478208315f6edaf10af999115eb29fa10d5601e9.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=-\\sqrt{y}+2$ and leaves through the upper function $x=-\\frac{y}{2}+3.$ So, we have $-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4482dfff4474145f9d9376488f2566949daf2ef7994717ff9e1346f596161a6"} {"question" "q-73534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le y\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3,\\,1\\le x\\le 3}"] ["math" "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le 2.5}"] ["math" "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3}"] ["math" "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+3\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}+2}"] ["math" "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,\\sqrt{y}\\le y\\le \\frac{y}{2},\\,1\\le x\\le 3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,-\\sqrt{y}+2\\le x\\le -\\frac{y}{2}+3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/627e7e102a0f16cb0c4946e42b48ad122299d729c5bc419293e258a3f2e1701e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/d7aa48c887d6fb1c3d0420867b7e74010fa93e16d7e24317e2cf214764e56113.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.5$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/ec632fa5f86d8d9b34b9ccf661a3219e965f289c28bf69d7d80eeeb46093e7ae.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4482dfff4474145f9d9376488f2566949daf2ef7994717ff9e1346f596161a6"} {"question" "q-73549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-73549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-168841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true regarding the triangle bounded between the lines $y=1-x,$ $y=x-1,$ and $x=0?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-168841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=1-x\\, & ⟹\\,x=1-y \\\\ y=x-1\\, & ⟹\\,x=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/assets/27503f983e3e02fa748bb8ef32966a6cd3b5fff29082ffaf3c10d0521b630e93.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 1-x}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1-|y|}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-168841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4482dfff4474145f9d9376488f2566949daf2ef7994717ff9e1346f596161a6"} {"question" "q-168841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-168841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I  and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"} {"question" "q-168841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I  and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048050/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd9ba61d437806442e2e98c607e6dabd3fa349228d90cf76eba2a439999a200e"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1704 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
